{title: Take Me Home, Country Roads}
{artist: John Denver}
{key: A}
{duration: 3:00}
{tempo: 82}


{start_of_part: Intro}
[G][G/D]
{end_of_part}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G] Almost Heaven[Em], West Virginia[D],
[D] Blue Ridge Mountains, [C]Shenandoah [G]River.
[G] Life is old there, [Em]older than the trees,
[D]younger than the mountains, [C]growin' like a br[G]eeze.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Country [G]Roads, take me [D]home, to the [Em]place I be[C]long
West Vir[G]ginia, mountain [D]mama, take me [C]home, country [G]roads.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G] All my memories[Em]  gather 'round her[D]
[D] Miner's lady, [C]stranger to blue [G]water.
[G] Dark and dusty, [Em]painted on the sky,
[D]Misty taste of moonshine, [C]teardrop in my [G]eye.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Country [G]Roads, take me [D]home, to the [Em]place I be[C]long
West Vir[G]ginia, mountain [D]mama, take me [C]home, country [G]roads.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Em] I hear her [D/F#]voice, in the [G]mornin' hour she calls me.
The [C]radio re[G]minds me of my [D]home far away.
And [Em]drivin' down the [F]road I get a [C]feelin' that I [G]should have been home 
[D]yesterday, yester[D7]day.
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_part: Outro}
Country [G]Roads, take me [D]home, to the [Em]place I be[C]long
West Vir[G]ginia, mountain [D]mama, take me [C]home, country [G]roads.

Country [G]Roads, take me [D]home, to the [Em]place I be[C]long
West Vir[G]ginia, mountain [D]mama, take me [C]home, country [G]roads.

Take me [D]home, (down) country [G]roads.
Take me [D]home, (down) country [G]roads.
{end_of_part}
